!Sample_submission_date = May 23 2022
!Sample_last_update_date = May 27 2022
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = primary CD8 T cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: primary CD8 T cells
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = days of_anti-cd3_stim: 6
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sgrna: ARID1A sg58
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sgrna delivery: Cas9 RNP
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = After activation, T cells were plated on chronic stimulation (anti-CD3 coated) plates to induce exhaustion
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Primary T cells were isolated from mouse spleen or human blood and cultured in media containing IL-2
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Live CD8+ T cells were isolated by FACS and subjected to ATAC-seq
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Omni ATAC-seq was performed as previously described (Corces et al Nature Methods 2017)
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were trimmed and quality filtered using fastp.
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were aligned to mm10 or hg38 using hisat2
!Sample_data_processing = Aligned reads were de-duplicated using Picard
!Sample_data_processing = Mitochondrial reads and Y chromosome reads were removed
!Sample_data_processing = Peaks were called for each sample using MACS2, merged into a union peak set, and the peak by count matrix was loaded into DESeq2 for differential analysis
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: mm10 or hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Genome tracks files were created by using the deduplicated reads, normalizing each sample using counts in TSS, and exported from R as bigwig files.
